{
  "platform": "react-vite-static",
  "implementationPath": {
    "rationale": "The objective (Plan a week of dinners on a $120 budget) requires a straightforward UI to capture budget and family size, and display a meal plan and shopping list. A static React SPA via Vite fits this perfectly. The logic for meal planning can run entirely client-side. The required primary language is javascript.",
    "recommendedIde": "VS Code with ESLint and Prettier.",
    "recommendedVibe": "Minimalist, functional React components with a clean, responsive layout. State managed via standard React hooks.",
    "hostingRationale": "Cloudflare Pages (requested) is ideal for a fast, globally distributed static site generated by Vite. It's cost-effective and integrates easily with GitHub.",
    "requirementTrace": [
      "objective -> src/App.jsx (Main container and logic orchestrator)",
      "io -> src/components/PlannerForm.jsx (Input form), src/components/MealPlan.jsx (Output display), src/components/ShoppingList.jsx (Output display)",
      "success -> src/utils/planner.js (Logic to ensure cost <= budget and 7 distinct meals)"
    ]
  },
  "collaboration": {
    "oracle": [],
    "dj": []
  },
  "framework": "React (Vite)",
  "language": "javascript",
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "package.json",
      "language": "json",
      "content": "{
  "name": "meal-planner",
  "private": true,
  "version": "0.0.0",
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "vite",
    "build": "vite build",
    "preview": "vite preview"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "react": "^18.2.0",
    "react-dom": "^18.2.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@vitejs/plugin-react": "^4.2.1",
    "vite": "^5.2.0"
  }
}"
    },
    {
      "path": "vite.config.js",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

// https://vitejs.dev/config/
export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
});"
    },
    {
      "path": "index.html",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/vite.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Budget Meal Planner</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.jsx"></script>
  </body>
</html>"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/main.jsx",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';
import App from './App.jsx';
import './index.css';

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <React.StrictMode>
    <App />
  </React.StrictMode>,
);"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/App.jsx",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "import React, { useState } from 'react';
import PlannerForm from './components/PlannerForm.jsx';
import MealPlan from './components/MealPlan.jsx';
import ShoppingList from './components/ShoppingList.jsx';
import { generatePlan } from './utils/planner.js';
import './App.css';

function App() {
  const [plan, setPlan] = useState(null);
  const [error, setError] = useState('');

  const handlePlanMeals = (budget, familySize) => {
    try {
      const newPlan = generatePlan(budget, familySize);
      setPlan(newPlan);
      setError('');
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err.message);
      setPlan(null);
    }
  };

  return (
    <div className="app-container">
      <header>
        <h1>Budget Meal Planner</h1>
      </header>
      <main>
        <PlannerForm onPlan={handlePlanMeals} />
        {error && <p className="error">{error}</p>}
        {plan && (
          <div className="results">
            <MealPlan days={plan.days} />
            <ShoppingList items={plan.shoppingList} />
          </div>
        )}
      </main>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/components/PlannerForm.jsx",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "import React, { useState } from 'react';

export default function PlannerForm({ onPlan }) {
  const [budget, setBudget] = useState(120);
  const [familySize, setFamilySize] = useState(4);

  const handleSubmit = (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    onPlan(Number(budget), Number(familySize));
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className="planner-form">
      <div className="form-group">
        <label htmlFor="budget">Budget ($):</label>
        <input
          type="number"
          id="budget"
          value={budget}
          onChange={(e) => setBudget(e.target.value)}
          min="1"
          required
        />
      </div>
      <div className="form-group">
        <label htmlFor="familySize">Family Size:</label>
        <input
          type="number"
          id="familySize"
          value={familySize}
          onChange={(e) => setFamilySize(e.target.value)}
          min="1"
          required
        />
      </div>
      <button type="submit">Plan Meals</button>
    </form>
  );
}"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/components/MealPlan.jsx",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "import React from 'react';

export default function MealPlan({ days }) {
  return (
    <section className="meal-plan">
      <h2>7-Day Meal Plan</h2>
      <ul>
        {days.map((day, index) => (
          <li key={index}>
            <strong>Day {index + 1}:</strong> {day.mealName} 
            <span className="cost">(Est. ${day.estimatedCost.toFixed(2)})</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  );
}"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/components/ShoppingList.jsx",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "import React from 'react';

export default function ShoppingList({ items }) {
  return (
    <section className="shopping-list">
      <h2>Shopping List</h2>
      <ul>
        {items.map((item, index) => (
          <li key={index}>
            {item.name} - {item.quantity} 
            <span className="cost">(${item.estimatedPrice.toFixed(2)})</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  );
}"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/utils/planner.js",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "/**
 * // TODO(code-one-plus): Objective: Plan a week of dinners on a $120 budget.
 * // TODO(code-one-plus): Success criteria: Total cost <= budget; 7 distinct meals.
 * 
 * This is a stub implementation. A real implementation would require a database
 * of recipes with ingredient costs scaled by family size.
 */
export function generatePlan(budget, familySize) {
  const recipes = [
    { name: 'Spaghetti Bolognese', baseCost: 15 },
    { name: 'Chicken Stir Fry', baseCost: 12 },
    { name: 'Vegetarian Chili', baseCost: 10 },
    { name: 'Tacos', baseCost: 14 },
    { name: 'Baked Salmon & Rice', baseCost: 20 },
    { name: 'Homemade Pizza', baseCost: 11 },
    { name: 'Lentil Soup', baseCost: 8 },
  ];

  // Very basic check: just ensuring we have 7 meals
  const days = recipes.slice(0, 7).map(recipe => {
      // Stub calculation for family size scaling, assumes baseCost is for family of 4
      const scalingFactor = familySize / 4;
      return {
          mealName: recipe.name,
          estimatedCost: recipe.baseCost * scalingFactor
      };
  });

  const totalEstimatedCost = days.reduce((sum, day) => sum + day.estimatedCost, 0);

  if (totalEstimatedCost > budget) {
       throw new Error(`Budget too low. Estimated minimum cost is $${totalEstimatedCost.toFixed(2)}`);
  }

  // Stub shopping list
  const shoppingList = [
    { name: 'Ground Beef', quantity: '1 lb', estimatedPrice: 5.00 * (familySize/4) },
    { name: 'Pasta', quantity: '1 box', estimatedPrice: 1.50 * (familySize/4) },
    { name: 'Mixed Veggies', quantity: '2 bags', estimatedPrice: 4.00 * (familySize/4) }
  ];

  return { days, shoppingList };
}"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/App.css",
      "language": "css",
      "content": ".app-container { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; font-family: sans-serif; }
.planner-form { display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; align-items: flex-end; }
.form-group { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.error { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.results { display: flex; gap: 40px; }
.meal-plan, .shopping-list { flex: 1; }
ul { list-style-type: none; padding: 0; }
li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; }
.cost { color: #666; font-size: 0.9em; margin-left: 10px; }"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/index.css",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #f9f9f9; color: #333; }"
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "language": "markdown",
      "content": "# Budget Meal Planner

Scaffolded static React SPA for planning 7 days of dinners based on budget and family size.

## Requirements Addressed
- **Objective:** Captures input to plan dinners.
- **I/O contract:** Inputs (budget, familySize) output days[] and shoppingList[].
- **Success criteria:** The planner utility ensures 7 distinct meals and validates total cost.

## Setup
1. `npm install`
2. `npm run dev`"
    }
  ],
  "manifest": {
    "framework": "react",
    "language": "javascript",
    "entrypoint": "src/main.jsx",
    "installCommand": "npm install",
    "runCommand": "npm run dev",
    "buildCommand": "npm run build",
    "deployTarget": "cloudflare-pages"
  },
  "notes": "Scaffolded React SPA via Vite. Includes UI forms and result displays. The meal planning logic in src/utils/planner.js is stubbed as the PDD lacks recipe data, but enforces the 7-meal rule and budget constraint."
}

